cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tvbench: a caller-side benchmark for telephony voice agents"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Almas
    given-names: Tahir
    affiliation: ICT Innovations
    email: tahir@ictinnovations.com
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22511442
repository-code: "https://github.com/ictinnovations/telephony-voice-agent-benchmark"
url: "https://www.ictinnovations.com/"
abstract: >-
  tvbench measures what a caller hears from a telephony voice agent rather than
  what the agent reports about itself. Acting as the Asterisk side of an
  AudioSocket connection, it timestamps every audio frame an agent returns and
  derives frame pacing, delivery burstiness, continuity within a turn, and
  barge-in cut latency. A reference agent with switchable defects provides a
  falsification pass so each metric is shown to move when the defect it targets
  is introduced.
keywords:
  - telephony
  - voice agent
  - benchmark
  - asterisk
  - audiosocket
  - latency
  - barge-in
  - speech interface
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-06"
